WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.480
What is this?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.440
I'll be joining the battle, too!

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.280
You'd better entertain me, at least a little.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.410
Open.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.450
A battle has begun. It's close.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.060
Is it Chi-chan?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.690
I don't know.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.780
Emergency.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:26.940
Let's hurry.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.380
We're back!

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.840
Taiyaki!

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.640
Wh-What is this?

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.750
What's going on?

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.520
That's right.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.940
I fought Selector battles here, too...

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.210
Chi-chan...

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.860
I'll go first.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.670
Unlock.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.380
Coin bet.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.860
Hello!

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.850
It's Aya, everyone's little sister!

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.310
Really? I'm doing support again?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.040
Turn end.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.270
You know how to use a key card, right?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.640
A second LRIG already...

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:55.760
Kiyoi!

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.880
I know.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.460
Unlock.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.720
Coin bet.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.700
It feels strange...

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.580
It's my own body, but it feels 
like it's been so long...

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.490
Donor.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:24.370
I'm going to ask for your help right away.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.050
Okay!

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.420
Wh-What do we do?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.790
Don't panic.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.180
We're just equal now.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:32.320
Aya.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.190
Coin bet.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.940
Yes!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.320
Holograph!

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.650
I'm sorry!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.210
Magical WIXOSS, Slow-ko!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.280
Now, attack. Go!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.330
I'm sorry!

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.740
Get yer butt in gear and go!

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.480
They're coming!

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.200
Donor, coin bet.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.310
Escape!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.310
Tch! What the hell are you doing, idiot?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.890
I'm sorry!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.440
She's strong...

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.480
You can tell, Chi-chan?

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.820
I still can't really remember 
the rules in detail,

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.320
but I can feel it...

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.750
She has a strong desire 
to win, no matter what.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.250
By the way, I want to check something.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.460
Are you fighting to beat me?

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:43.920
What do you mean?

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.940
I mean you can't win like this.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.370
You need to work a little harder,

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.890
little bitch!

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.460
No, Kiyoi!

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.730
Don't let him provoke you!
It's what he wants!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.940
Don't worry. I know.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.790
But what Carnival is saying makes sense.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.150
I can't win like this.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.990
Kiyoi, you're not planning to 
become the third LRIG, are you?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.950
Don't! It's too dangerous!

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.900
If I want to win, I need to gamble.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.290
Okay.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.000
Unlock.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.460
Coin bet.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.300
Wh-What?

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.560
Donor?

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.010
Kiyoi, Donor just...

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:36.100
So you can only have two 
LRIGs on the field at once?

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.040
Too bad.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.020
Looks like your plan didn't work out.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.180
It's not really a problem.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.140
I know the rules now.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:45.980
Piruluk.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:46.490
Right.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.200
Coin bet.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.950
Catharsis.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.800
Mizushima Kiyoi...

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.990
This power is a problem.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:01.750
I guess it's time.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.370
If I decide to crush you, 
I'm going to crush you hard.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.990
So you can never stand up again.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.060
Unlock.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.220
Coin bet.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.360
No way...

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.730
Why can Carnival use three LRIGs at once?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.950
I'm special!

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.600
Now, let's end this.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.660
Slow-ko, Aya.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.790
Summon Hurricane, Tsunawata.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.780
Now, how will you stop me?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:57.100
What happens to a Selector when 
they run out of coins, I wonder?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.720
I can't want to find out, Mizushima Kiyoi.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.610
H-Hey, what's wrong? Let's finish it.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:11.990
Now, of all times...

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.750
What just happened?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:32.200
A forced ending to the game 
without someone else interfering?

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.160
And Carnival is gone?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.760
Are we... saved? I guess?

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:43.060
If that battle had gone on...

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.440
I would've lost.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.650
Chi-chan!

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.860
Suzu?

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:54.160
Are you okay?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.060
You haven't fought yet, have you?

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.330
Y-Yeah.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:01.710
Carnival came after her, 
but Kiyoi came in at the last second.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.140
Kiyoi-chan did?

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:04.880
Wait... Huh?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:05.860
Donor-san?

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:06.920
Shock.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.340
Why did you become an LRIG again?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.540
Oh, well, um...

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:25.150
What do you plan to do with all these LRIGs?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.630
Your style is to become an LRIG 
yourself and fight, right?

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.110
You don't even need other LRIGs.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.880
At least give back Midoriko and Hanayo-san.

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.110
I can't.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:42.500
The rule is you can't give someone 
an LRIG unless you lose a battle.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.610
Are you telling me to lose deliberately?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.740
That girl with the glasses 
just needs to get stronger.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.080
Strong enough to beat me.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.260
The weak don't have the 
right to say anything.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.220
What is it you're after?

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.100
I want to defeat that monster.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.290
Just do it already!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.620
Um, I'm with Pizza Hattori.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.930
I have the pizza you ordered.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.580
Thanks.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.100
Right on time.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.890
Th-Thanks.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.870
Eat. You passed.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.800
What? Are you screwing with me?

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.860
I like the self-destructive way you fight.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.460
You want to fight strong opponents, right?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.820
If you help me, I'll set up 
as many fights as you want.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.780
What are you about to do?

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.760
Make the Selector battles more exciting.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:11.530
Make them fun and cheerful, 
the way I like them.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.640
I can't beat him like this.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:25.310
I'm going to fight more battles 
and beat him, no matter what.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.200
What are you thinking?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:36.870
I don't want you interfering in my battles. 
You're messing up my plans.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.360
It won't open.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.780
The door won't open.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.420
The door? What do you mean?

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.870
Don't you just need enough 
keys to open the door?

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.600
It's broken.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.610
The keyhole is broken.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.400
The keyhole? What do you mean?

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:58.610
A new keyhole will appear soon.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.920
The first door was...

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.500
The door to the outside.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:04.590
The door to the girls.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:07.240
They opened the door and left.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.270
The girls left.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.640
The girls?

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.730
Bring the keyhole here.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.650
The keyhole. Bring it here.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.520
Understanding.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:33.200
It seems Carnival is indeed a unique being.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.250
Chi-chan...

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:40.970
I really don't want you getting 
involved in these Selector battles.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.410
Suzu...

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.480
I don't know what will happen 
if you lose your memories,

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.120
but I know you won't escape 
unscathed this time.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.890
I don't want you to get involved 
in something so dangerous.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.650
Thank you, Suzu.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:57.360
But I feel the same way.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:01.660
If the battles are that dangerous, 
I don't want you to get involved.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:04.480
Especially if you're saying it's for me...

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.080
I couldn't take that.

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.900
Chi-chan...

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.040
You're both very kind.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.510
Suggestion.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:14.590
If you both want the same thing,

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.590
why not settle it with a battle?

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:18.000
A battle?

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:20.560
If you can't avoid the battles,

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.930
the best thing to do is 
minimize the risk of defeat

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.220
and maximize your chance of winning.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.360
You two can battle, and the stronger 
is entrusted with the other's LRIG

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.060
to maximize their chance 
of getting what they want.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.790
Entrust your LRIG...

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.600
...to the stronger?

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:40.360
But if you battle, 
one of you will lose a coin.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.690
Naturally.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.620
But if you fight someone you can trust,

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:47.320
you can fight them again 
to get the coin back.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:51.790
That's the neverending draw plan 
that Shou-chan talked about.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.930
It carries some risk,

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:58.020
but I think it's a very effective 
method of buying some time.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:03.640
But Chi-chan, you've lost most of your 
memories about the battles, right?

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.220
If you fight Suzu right now...

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.560
But I still need to win,

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.570
or Suzu will fight.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.100
So I have to win, right?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.580
Help me, Meru.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.080
Chi-chan...

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.020
Right.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.730
Chi-chan, hold up your card.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.820
Open!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:39.460
We don't want to lose any coins, 
so neither of us should do a coin bet.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.110
A coin bet?

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:44.020
The technique Mizushima-san 
and her opponent used.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.800
If there's anything you 
don't understand, ask me.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.680
Thanks, Meru.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.930
Here I go, Chi-chan.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:53.390
Grow.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:58.060
Play Arm, Kukuri, Nunchaku.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.770
Turn end.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.980
It's my turn... Um...

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.490
I'll place some ENER and attack.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.610
Chi-chan, you haven't grown yet.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.600
Chi-chan?

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.700
Suzuko...

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.450
I know.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.640
It's my turn.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:16.930
Full attack.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.160
Riru, attack!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.810
Meru! I'm sorry... I...

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.060
It's okay.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.760
Do you remember a little now?

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:33.050
You and I fought together.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:34.440
Meru...

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:41.350
Yeah.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.570
You were always there for me.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.340
And you still are.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.350
You fight with your LRIG.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:52.000
That's what WIXOSS is.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:52.910
Yeah.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:54.870
Meru, grow!

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:57.910
Elegant Moonlit Evening!

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.210
Three Orders, Five Explanations!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.000
<i>It's my third time battling Chi-chan.</i>

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:10.300
<i>The first time, Chi-chan was 
trying to get rid of me.</i>

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:15.090
<i>The second, I was trying to protect her.</i>

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.740
<i>And the third...</i>

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:22.690
Chi-chan, for the first time, 
I'm having fun battling!

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.730
ARTS: Grab the Chestnut from the Fire!

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:27.420
I'm having fun, too, Suzu!

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.110
Guard!

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.990
They both look so happy...

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.200
Envy.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:44.250
This is what a battle should be, right?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.960
Chi-chan, are you okay?

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.670
Yeah.

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.270
It's a little strange.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:57.090
I've lost all my memories of the 
previous Selector battles, but...

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.360
I want to keep going.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.140
But...

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.940
Thank you, Suzu.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.820
Chi-chan...

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.500
Once these Selector battles are over,

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.780
let's play WIXOSS again!

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.410
See Through the Fiery Ambition!

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.800
I'm sorry, Meru.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.920
I lost.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:31.560
No, it was fun fighting with you.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.410
Leave the rest to us.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.490
Yeah. Thanks.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.030
Suzu, take care of Meru, okay?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.240
Chi-chan...

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:59.490
Can you still tell me that Suzuko-san 
should get her memories back?

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:03.410
Leave it to me.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.820
But I'm not planning on sitting this out.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:11.160
I lost my LRIG,

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.840
but I think I can help you with 
things other than the battles.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.050
I want to help you as you fight.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.490
Then you're one of us now.

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:22.700
One of you?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.250
Acknowledgement.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.420
I welcome you.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.020
Glad to have you, Morikawa Chinatsu-san.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:29.860
Yeah!

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.320
Panties, panties!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.650
Hey, fold them up!

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.220
Jeez.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.380
I knew it! It's you, Hitoe!

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.500
I saw you from the veranda.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.290
Did you need something?

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.220
Huh? Why do you have two bags?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.900
Hitoe? Wait! Hitoe!

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:13.920
What's wrong?

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.190
Did something happen?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.950
I'm about to have some hot milk with Tama.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.120
Want to join me?

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.120
Help me...

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.840
Help me, Ruuko...

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.910
Hitoe...

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.940
Huh? You and Yuzuki were chosen as Selectors?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:57.740
A new series of Selector battles has begun.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:02.400
With the new rules, Selectors become LRIGs,

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.680
and if you lose, your LRIG is taken away...

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:08.620
You mean Yuzuki became an LRIG, 
and her opponent took her?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.070
Why didn't you tell me?

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:15.250
You can't just not tell me!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.220
I didn't want to get you involved...

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:22.970
You or Tama-chan...

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:29.420
That voice... I know it.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:01.760
Hitoe...

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:03.970
Yuzuki...

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.100
Ruu...

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.430
I...

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.740
Ruu, I'll...

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:17.980
Tama!

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.820
I'll help you!

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:22.610
Tama-chan?

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.770
I want to help Yuzuki!

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.260
And you, too!

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:29.960
Because you're my dear friends!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:30.620
But...

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.300
Do you know what you're saying, Tama?

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:35.580
Yeah.

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.800
I heard a voice.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.140
Again and again...

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:40.790
A voice calling me.

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:43.720
If I can save everyone, I'll fight!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.090
I'll do the battles!

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.440
But...

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:47.430
It'll be okay!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.060
Everyone is with me!

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:53.130
Ruu, and Hitoe, and Yuzuki!

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:58.110
Tama...

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:02.570
We're together... together forever...

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:06.980
So I'll fight with you.

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.330
Let's fight together, Tama!

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:12.460
Yeah!

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:16.020
Tama!

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:17.190
Tama-chan?

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.050
Tama...

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.630
Ruuko, you were chosen to be a Selector?

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:28.070
Let's do our best, Ruu!

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:30.350
Let's save everyone together!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:32.300
Yeah!

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.300
Just as planned.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:45.150
Now, at last, all the pieces are in place.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:47.990
And...

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.170
the keyhole, too.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.960
Determination / Warmth and Pain

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:28.960
Everything went well because 
Kiyoi-chan was here.

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:30.880
Let's play with Kiyoi-chan!

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.960
I want to see Mizushima 
Kiyoi-chan, no matter what!

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:34.660
I want to see her, no matter what!

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:37.240
If I do, I can become happy!

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:38.470
Let's hide!

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:40.980
Attachment / Trick and Trap

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:40.980
Attachment / Trick and Trap.
